silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_03_pullback_vs_pushforward_sections_01_pushforward_as_information_flow_yoneda_hom_leg silm:hasExample "In 'PushforwardAsInformationFlowYonedaHomLeg', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, the functor F sends Mittens to F(Mittens), giving the central object of the transport diagram its clinic-side image.; also, the functor F sends each household typed arrow to a clinic typed arrow with matching domain and codomain assignments." .
